@id n3_thomas
# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, in the infirmary (night 3). Tall, thin, stooped, gentle deep-set eyes, fingers stained from his herbs; he hums at his mortar.
# Your first ally. He tells you what he has noticed, always about someone else. (He leads the cult. Nothing here says so.)
# At supper Ranulf offers his remedy and Thomas warns you off it; the headaches answer sets that up.
# Claims: n3_thomas_prior (misleading): the prior was up the tower stair first, which is so; he says it to point at an innocent man. Pressing is the right read.
== start
(Thomas is at his bench, grinding something in a mortar and humming. He stops when he sees you, and smiles.)
Thomas {warm}: Alric. Come in. You slept, I hope? You've the look of a man who dreamed.
-> topics

== again
(Thomas looks up from his mortar. His fingers are stained green to the knuckle.)
Thomas {warm}: Back again? Sit. I'm only grinding.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n3_thomas_headaches] My head aches, Brother Thomas. It won't let up. -> headaches
* [if not n3_thomas_anselm] How is Brother Anselm? -> anselm
* [if not n3_thomas_tower] Did you know the brother in the bell tower? -> tower

== headaches [set n3_thomas_headaches]
Thomas {warm}: Behind the eyes? Worse when you wake?
(He tilts your face to the window and looks into one eye, then the other.)
Thomas {warm, nod}: It's the night hours. A body takes a month to learn them. Sleep with your shutter closed, and eat.
Thomas {warm}: And if anyone offers you physic for it, come to me first. Physic is my trade.
-> topics

== anselm [set n3_thomas_anselm]
Thomas {warm}: Quieter since the tower. He asks after you. Old porters never stop keeping the gate.
Thomas {warm, still}: Don't let him frighten you, Alric. His mind wanders at night. He hears things.
-> topics

== tower [set n3_thomas_tower] [claim n3_thomas_prior misleading]
Thomas {sad}: Bede. I'm sorry you were the one who found him. A hard thing, on your second night.
Thomas {grave, nod}: Father Abbot says the demon. I've seen what I've seen in this house. I don't argue with him.
Thomas {warm, still}: Only I wonder about the prior. He was up the tower stair before any of us. Quick, for a man woken by a bell.
* [believe] Then I'll watch him, brother. -> prior_believed
* [press] Before any of you? Who saw him go up? -> prior_pressed

== prior_believed
Thomas {warm, nod}: Quietly, Alric. Watch, and say nothing to him. He's the prior, and you're the porter.
-> topics

== prior_pressed
Thomas {warm, still}: I say only what I saw. Make of it what you like.
(He takes up his pestle again.)
-> topics

== leave
Thomas {warm}: Rest before supper, Alric. The nights are long.
